        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "fix(cron): support current and session: targets in initial delivery resolution",
        "body": "## What Problem This Solves\n\n`resolveInitialCronDelivery` in `src/cron/service/initial-delivery.ts` only checks `sessionTarget === \"isolated\"` when deciding whether to inject default `{ mode: \"announce\" }` delivery. All other cron code paths already treat `\"isolated\"`, `\"current\"`, and `\"session:\"` as equivalent for this purpose, creating an inconsistency.\n\n## Why This Change Was Made\n\nAfter #98947 restored persistent session targets, the three sessionTarget values are treated identically in:\n- `delivery-plan.ts:106-114` — `isDetachedOutputJob` check\n- `normalize.ts:680-684` — `isDetachedDeliveryJob` check\n- `jobs.ts:288-298` — `isIsolatedLike` check\n\nBut `initial-delivery.ts` was not updated, so cron jobs created with `--session-target current` or `--session-target session:...` would not get the default announce delivery at creation time.\n\n## User Impact\n\nUsers creating cron jobs with `sessionTarget: \"current\"` or `\"session:\"` may miss delivery announcements.\n\n## Evidence\n\n**Real behavior proof — reproduced via node:**\n```\nInput:  sessionTarget=\"current\", payload.kind=\"agentTurn\"\nOLD:    undefined  <- missing default announce delivery\nNEW:    {mode:\"announce\"}  <- consistent with delivery-plan, normalize, jobs\n```\n\n**Validation:**\n- tsgo typecheck: passed\n- `pnpm test src/cron/service/`: 152 tests (15 files) passed\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)",
